    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Phibsboro are delighted to present to the market 4 Parkview Grove, a well presented ground floor one bedroom apartment ideally positioned in this mature and well established development. Constructed in the early 2000s, this spacious apartment extends to approximately 52 sq.m. and benefits from generously proportioned living accommodation throughout. The property also enjoys the added benefit of a private wrap around patio/balcony, providing an excellent outdoor space that is accessed directly from the apartment.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall leading into a bright and spacious open plan kitchen, living and dining area. The kitchen is well laid out with ample fitted storage and worktop space, while the adjoining living and dining area provides a comfortable and versatile space for both everyday living and entertaining. The apartment also benefits from a separate utility room, providing useful additional storage and laundry space. The generous double bedroom offers good proportions and built in storage, while the bathroom is finished in a clean and modern style. The overall accommodation is presented in a clean and sleek style, with well maintained interiors throughout. Further benefits include electric heating and a BER rating of D2.\n\nParkview Grove is conveniently located within easy reach of a wide range of amenities and services. The surrounding area offers an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and recreational facilities, while nearby Phibsborough and Glasnevin provide further amenities. The location is well served by public transport, with numerous bus routes operating in the surrounding area and easy access to Dublin city centre. The property is also well positioned for access to the M50 and wider road network, making it an ideal choice for both owner occupiers and investors alike."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2.84m x 1.17m\nA welcoming entrance hall with sleek flooring. The hallway is bright and well presented, creating a pleasant first impression upon entering the property.\n\nKitchen/Living/Dining Room - 2.65m x 2.35m & 3.45m x 5.53m\nA generously proportioned open plan space combining the kitchen, living and dining areas. The kitchen is well fitted with ample storage and worktop space, while the living and dining areas provide excellent room for both relaxation and entertaining. An abundance of natural light fills the room, with access leading directly out to the private wrap around patio. The outdoor area is enclosed by hedging and timber fencing, providing a good degree of privacy.\n\nUtility Room - 1.73m x 1.33m\nLocated to the rear of the kitchen, the separate utility room provides excellent additional storage and practical space. The room is plumbed for a washing machine and features a countertop, ideal for laundry use or additional storage.\n\nShower Room - 1.81m x 2.35m\nA well maintained, fully tiled bathroom comprising a WC, wash hand basin and shower unit, with tiled flooring and walls throughout.\n\nBedroom - 2.84m x 4.26m\nA generously sized double bedroom featuring fitted wardrobes and ample space for additional bedroom furniture. The room benefits from excellent natural light and direct door access to the private patio, allowing for easy access to the outdoor space.\n\nPatio/Balcony - 7.06m x 5.51m\nA particularly attractive feature of the property is the private wrap around patio, which provides a generous outdoor area adjoining the apartment. The patio is enclosed by timber fencing and established hedging, creating a private and secluded setting. The space offers ample room for outdoor seating, planting and entertaining.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> 1 Bed, 1 Bath Ground Floor Apartment</li><li> Approx. 52 sq. m.</li><li> BER Rating D2</li><li> Constructed in the Early 2000s</li><li> Private Outdoor Space with Hedging and Timber Fencing</li><li> Situated within easy reach of Poppintree Park, Charlestown Shopping Centre, IKEA and DCU, with a wide selection of shops, cafés and everyday amenities nearby.</li><li> Conveniently located close to a number of bus routes providing regular services towards Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. The property also offers easy access to the M50, providing connectivity to Dublin Airport and the wider Dublin road network, while the M1 is readily accessible for journeys northbound.</ul>"
      },
